Merge Sort Unique
=================

Write a function:

    def merge_sort_unique(lists: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]

Merge all the inner lists into one, remove duplicates, and return the values
sorted in ascending order.

Examples:
    merge_sort_unique([[1, 3, 5], [2, 3, 6], [1, 7]]) -> [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7]
    merge_sort_unique([[2, 2], [2]]) -> [2]
    merge_sort_unique([[], []]) -> []
    merge_sort_unique([]) -> []
